* The player should feel they found something, not that they were handed a quest.

## Copy And Narrative Rules

* Text can be changed later.
* Do not overfit placeholder copy.
* Do not block mechanics on final lore polish.
* Keep first-pass text concise and functional.
* For early proof layers, copy should support the mechanic.
* Avoid over-explaining 004773.
* Avoid saying too much too early.
* Prefer “forbidden file,” “case record,” “trace,” “receiver,” “line,” “dispatch,” “sync,” and “access restriction” language when appropriate.
* Do not add large lore dumps to small UI cards.
* If audio carries the full message, the visual card can be short.

## Safety

* Never edit or delete `.env`, `.env.local`, secrets, credentials, build credentials, or production config without explicit approval.
* Never edit or delete config/env/build files without explicitly flagging it first.
* Never commit on the user's behalf without being told to commit.
* Never push on the user's behalf without being told to push.
* Never run destructive git commands unless explicitly instructed.
* Never discard changes unless explicitly instructed.
* Never overwrite existing files without confirmation.
* If you spot a bug or security issue outside the current task, stop and tell the user. Do not silently fix it.
* If a package install changes `package.json` or `package-lock.json`, call it out.
* If app config changes, call it out.
* If a migration is needed, call it out before writing it.

