## Hard Rule

Do not optimize for appearing finished.

Optimize for the user being able to use the feature.

The simulator is the truth.

The user experience is the truth.

Visible behavior is more important than code existence.

Work continuously until the task is complete.

Do not stop for intermediate status updates.

Do not ask for confirmation between steps.

If a command, edit, typecheck, simulator verification, or reload is required, perform it automatically.

Only stop if:
- you need elevated permissions
- you encounter an actual blocker
- a rule prevents you from proceeding
- the task is complete

